      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-159786",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, X_{3}, X_{4}$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_{i}\u223cN(\u03b8, 1)$, where $\u03b8$ is an unknown mean. Given that the likelihood function of the sample $-1.2, 0.4, 2.2, 0.8$ is\n$L(\u03b8) = \\frac{1}{4\u03c0^{2}}e^{g (\u03b8)}$,\nwhat is the expression for $g(\u03b8)$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
